## Develop and install

{% if tool_ui_kind == "in-app" %}
Build the frontend first:

```shell
cd frontend
yarn install
yarn build
cd ..
```

Commit `frontend/yarn.lock` and
`src/{{ distribution_name | replace('-', '_') }}/static/frontend/tool.js`.
The source distribution includes the frontend sources; the wheel includes the
compiled bundle.
{% endif %}

Add the plugin to the datalab checkout's root `plugins.toml`:

```toml
dependencies = [{{ distribution_name | tojson }}]

[tool.uv.sources]
{{ distribution_name }} = { path = "../{{ distribution_name }}", editable = true }
```

Then install it and restart the API:

```shell
cd pydatalab
uv run invoke dev.install
```

## How it accesses datalab

{% if tool_ui_kind == "in-app" %}
The provider serves one *in-app frontend bundle*. datalab authenticates the
*provider route*, and the component uses `window.datalabToolSdk.api` with the
current *browser session*. Normal datalab API permissions still decide which
data the user can access.
{% if add_item_table_action %}

The **{{ item_table_action_label }}** table action is available in
`{{ item_table_action_tables | join("`, `") }}` for selections of
{{ item_table_action_min_items }} to {{ item_table_action_max_items }} items.
Read its ordered refcodes with `datalabToolSdk.selection.current()` and load the
items through permission-aware API routes.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
The provider issues a single-use *launch code*. Its protected exchange route
returns a *tool access token*, which the standalone page keeps only in
memory and sends to normal datalab API routes as `DATALAB-API-KEY`.
{% endif %}

## Administrator trust

Tool plugins are trusted Python packages. In-app bundles are also trusted
JavaScript running inside the signed-in datalab application. An administrator
must review the source, dependencies, lockfiles, compiled assets, maintainers,
and release provenance before installation and every upgrade.

See the datalab
[Tools documentation](https://docs.datalab-org.io/tools/) and
[glossary](https://docs.datalab-org.io/tools-glossary/) for the complete
contracts and security model.
